# Confirmed live on production (guthrieent.com, the Cloudflare Pages
# deployment): /CLAUDE.md and /schema.sql serve their real file content
# (text/markdown and application/x-sql respectively) to anyone. Everything
# else checked -- .git/*, functions/**/*.js -- turned out to be a false
# alarm: this project's Pages deployment already falls back to the
# homepage (200, text/html) for those, same as any other unmatched path,
# because Pages has always excluded .git and functions/ from what it
# uploads. CLAUDE.md and schema.sql are ordinary repo-root files with no
# such special-casing, so they're served like any other static asset.
#
# .assetsignore (added for the separate Workers-static-assets deployment)
# has no effect here -- Pages doesn't read that file. This is the
# Pages-native way to stop answering a specific path with its real
# content: matching requests get the homepage back, reported as 404.
/CLAUDE.md / 404
/schema.sql / 404
